import{_ as t,o as i,c as a,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const c=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 406 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Three-Realms-Setting Analysis: Closed World and Civilizational Limitation","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 406 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Three-Realms-Setting Analysis: Closed World and Civilizational Limitation","no":406,"module":2,"tags":["Manghuang Ji","Three Realms","Closed World","Civilizational Limitation","Geographic Setting"],"related":["80-Plane Theory and Classification","78-Cross-Plane Exploration Era","05-Myriad-Ranks Joint Progress Basic Program"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0406_模块2-莽荒纪-三界设定分析-封闭世界与文明局限.md","filePath":"en/0406_模块2-莽荒纪-三界设定分析-封闭世界与文明局限.md"}'),o={name:"en/0406_模块2-莽荒纪-三界设定分析-封闭世界与文明局限.md"};function s(r,e,l,d,h,m){return i(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-406-manghuang-system-decomposition-·-three-realms-setting-analysis-closed-world-and-civilizational-limitation" tabindex="-1">Entry 406 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Three-Realms-Setting Analysis: Closed World and Civilizational Limitation <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-406-manghuang-system-decomposition-·-three-realms-setting-analysis-closed-world-and-civilizational-limitation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 406 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Three-Realms-Setting Analysis: Closed World and Civilizational Limitation&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Manghuang Ji Full Decomposition (Entry 11) | Benchmark base: Documents 80, 78, 05</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-three-realms-are-not-a-cosmos-but-a-yard-with-very-high-walls" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Three Realms are not a cosmos, but a yard with very high walls <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-three-realms-are-not-a-cosmos-but-a-yard-with-very-high-walls" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Three Realms are not a cosmos, but a yard with very high walls&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the republican axiom of Myriad Races requires Myriad Ranks 99% full coverage; hyper-multiverse full openness is the mandatory core. Manghuang&#39;s &quot;Three Realms&quot; (Heaven, Earth, Human) is the early main stage — it looks complete, but is actually a closed yard with extremely high walls: mortal, immortal, divine three layers separated; mortals hard to ascend, immortals never look back. This entry uses Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s plane theory to examine this &quot;closed world&quot;&#39;s civilizational limitation. The law-first axiom reminds: geographic setting boundaries must legislate first, otherwise late will be redrawn by plot. Protagonist uniqueness dependency = high-leaning-medium. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s judging base has been upgraded to the six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Closed Three Realms&#39; energy waste lies in &quot;vertical blockade&quot;: Heaven Realm&#39;s rich qi open only to immortals; Human Realm&#39;s thin qi supports mortals; no energy circulation between the two layers. Heaven&#39;s surplus energy cannot feed back to Human; Human&#39;s vitality cannot rise upward — the entire Three Realms&#39; energy flow is cut. <strong>A closed system with a broken loop inevitably exhausts from within.</strong></p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Closed Three Realms&#39; regression logic:</p><ol><li><strong>Upward channel locked</strong>: mortal cultivation relies on spiritual roots, adventures, immortal fortune; channel extremely narrow; Human Realm civilization forever stuck at low energy</li><li><strong>Heaven complacent</strong>: immortals long reside in Heaven, know not mortal hardship, no duty to feed back; Heaven and Human drift apart</li><li><strong>Boundary = ceiling</strong>: outside Three Realms at first &quot;unknowable,&quot; later opened by plot; early everyone thought Three Realms is all; this cognitive limitation itself is civilization&#39;s ceiling</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Behind Three-Realms setting is the monopoly of &quot;channel right&quot;:</p><ul><li><strong>Immortal-mortal partition</strong>: immortals have a duty not to interfere in the human world; essentially keeping the human world as a &quot;lower quarter&quot; penned</li><li><strong>Ascend = abandon</strong>: after Ji Ning ascends, Human Realm to him is only memory, no construction duty</li><li><strong>Channel decided by strong ones</strong>: who can go to heaven, who must stay; rules interpreted by Heaven&#39;s strong ones</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Manghuang Closed Three Realms</th><th>Anchor-Symbiosis Open Planes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Immortal-mortal partition, energy flow cut</td><td>Plane theory and classification: each layer&#39;s energy circulation interconnected</td></tr><tr><td>Ascend = abandon lower realm</td><td>Cross-Plane Exploration Era: strong ones feed back to old realm</td></tr><tr><td>Channel monopolized by strong ones</td><td>Myriad-Ranks Joint Progress Basic Program: all beings have upward qualification</td></tr><tr><td>Three Realms = all (cognitive limitation)</td><td>Cross-plane anchor connection: open not closed</td></tr><tr><td>Heaven complacent no feedback</td><td>Strong-one post-duty system; lifespans feed back to Myriad Ranks</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate Manghuang&#39;s Three Realms &quot;immortal—mortal&quot; two-layer energy-flow model</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: compare &quot;closed partition,&quot; &quot;semi-open,&quot; &quot;Anchor energy interconnection injected&quot; three structures</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: Human Realm average energy, immortal-mortal channel flow, civilization&#39;s overall energy utilization</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: quantified conclusion — under closed model Human Realm energy does not rise in a millennium; under interconnection model two layers&#39; energy rise in step</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: medium-low</strong>. Three-Realms boundary early &quot;impassable,&quot; late casually opened; outside world continuously appended by new setting</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: medium-high</strong>. Three-Realms geography redrawn several times; &quot;outside Three Realms&quot; definition expands with inflation</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: high-leaning-medium</strong>. Three-Realms order maintained by top strong ones; boundary opening decided by Ji Ning&#39;s plot needs</li></ul><p>Three-Realms closure also has a psychological consequence: it makes Three-Realms residents truly believe they are the cosmos&#39;s all. This cognitive limitation is scarier than physical walls — when a civilization believes it has reached the top, it loses the drive to explore outward. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Cross-Plane Exploration Era is the opposite: it tells you from day one the cosmos is open, layers must flow. The closed world&#39;s greatest loss is not a few fewer cultivation quotas, but the entire civilization&#39;s imagination nailed dead by an invisible wall.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: vertical blockade causes Heaven&#39;s surplus energy unable to feed back to Human</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: immortal-mortal partition is structural stripping of mortals&#39; upward right</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo at least opened class within humankind; Manghuang did not even open immortal-mortal two layers</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: outside Three Realms Myriad Ranks early not recognized as &quot;world residents&quot; at all</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: a closed yard is fundamentally opposed to a hyper-multiverse full-open cosmology</li></ul><p>Three-Realms closure also manufactures a false sense of security. Heaven residents think outside the wall is unknown, so rest content; until the wall is opened by plot, they discover outside already strong ones like clouds. This &quot;suddenly seeing the world&quot; shock is itself a fuse of civilizational regression — because it was unprepared. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s open-plane view is the opposite: it from the start acknowledges outside the wall is a world, encourages residents to explore with a plan. Closed is not safety, but hoarding accidents until they explode all at once.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Three-Realms setting&#39;s problem is not &quot;small,&quot; but &quot;closed.&quot; A yard that pens mortals at low energy and locks immortals in complacency, however beautiful, is still only a yard. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s plane view is open — layers must flow, strong and weak must feed back, civilization will not exhaust from within.</p><p>In the final analysis, Manghuang Ji · Three-Realms-setting analysis · closed world and civilizational limitation described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./405_模块2-莽荒纪-设定自洽度评估-中低自洽度的量化.html">Entry 405 · Setting-Self-Consistency Assessment</a> · <a href="./407_模块2-莽荒纪-混沌仙界设定-阶层固化的终极形态.html">Entry 407 · Chaos Immortal Realm Setting</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/80-位面理论与分类.html">80-Plane Theory and Classification</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',28)])])}const g=t(o,[["render",s]]);export{c as __pageData,g as default};
